     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">It is possible. It would be nice to explain it with your own data set. Here I try to explain it with one of my dataset<div><br></div><div>I have a methylRawList object <i>yng_vs_aged</i>. This has ten samples. If I have to change the name of any one of the sample, say 2nd sample. I will do the following:</div><div><br></div><div>yng_vs_aged[[2]]@<a href=\"http://sample.id\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://sample.id&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793233752978000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2q2bunT8ZfvUCYVnpHswA-\">sample.id</a>=&quot;changed_id&quot;</div><div><br></div><div>That should help you!</div><div hspace=\"streak-pt-mark\" style=\"max-height:1px\"><img style=\"width:0px;max-height:0px\" src=\"https://ci4.googleusercontent.com/proxy/kOU1WFppGD9OD8JinLq0C3jKp-hK0wNIN9_40sFDiqvAbLK0aKMiOmAiRCThxtli4fjIDxZMD9fBHktdyvoKbcT4VUSJ8QC-cMBIMpVm_W62g54fecNickW_dQZ4U-GZcj-rLPBlzarmKjXXVu7Dw88EUThK4IiWT3jXhiZ-2RVjQxIrKzr04ikM3EKDmO3mChB_fRbweCI=s0-d-e1-ft#https://mailfoogae.appspot.com/t?sender=aa2FseWFua3B5QGdtYWlsLmNvbQ%3D%3D&amp;type=zerocontent&amp;guid=ef9d457a-1e07-4233-b0ff-d02e0d85d2f5\"><font color=\"#ffffff\" size=\"1\">ᐧ</font></div></div><div class=\"gmail_extra\"><br clear=\"all\"><div><div class=\"gmail_signature\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div><div dir=\"ltr\">Regards,<br>Kalyan<br><br></div></div></div></div></div>\r\n<br><div class=\"gmail_quote\"></div></div>"
